                "forms": [],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "9927ccb6-5a1d-3fd1-be3a-9de362bdb142",
                        "entry_id": "42f639c0-017c-32a3-89e9-c86ceedc8db6",
                        "glosses": [
                            "przebrzmiały, już niemodny"
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "04121f30-b5f6-4a20-b5ad-a02e55a40885",
                                "sense_id": "9927ccb6-5a1d-3fd1-be3a-9de362bdb142",
                                "text": "Buty ze szpicami są passé."
                            }
                        ],
                        "sense_index_json": "\"1.1\""
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "1508f028-b3cb-40db-8a6c-56d041600e7f",
                        "source_entry_id": "42f639c0-017c-32a3-89e9-c86ceedc8db6",
                        "source_sense_id": "9927ccb6-5a1d-3fd1-be3a-9de362bdb142",
                        "target_lang_word": "old-fashioned",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "old-fashioned",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "f392e96b-ef83-3164-9733-00d30270545b",
                                        "entry_id": "0f822407-f74e-3586-bb6b-944b98803345",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Of an object, outdated or no longer in vogue."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "874d4c4e-6bcd-4319-bbab-510305a2d43f",
                                                "sense_id": "f392e96b-ef83-3164-9733-00d30270545b",
                                                "text": "My bike is old-fashioned but it gets me around."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "f21ae721-0655-4ddb-bc6f-84ac391f3c24",
                                                "sense_id": "f392e96b-ef83-3164-9733-00d30270545b",
                                                "text": "Miss Menie, we should mention, has a commendable desire to sell her oldest-fashioned articles first; indeed, we believe that something of the sort has always been common among mercers. It is true, that the most conscientious of the trade make a point, in such cases, to say nothing of the fashionableness of the patterns, but in proportion to the care with which they do this, they enlarge on the good qualities of the texture and durability."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "173b3d98-c702-4885-9479-b3389f26ad0b",
                                                "sense_id": "f392e96b-ef83-3164-9733-00d30270545b",
                                                "text": "She was seated in a low old-fashioned arm-chair, directly below a portrait of herself, that had been taken just before her first visit to London."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "0f4d8c9b-1e7f-4cae-a0bd-1cc32bb64907",
                                                "sense_id": "f392e96b-ef83-3164-9733-00d30270545b",
                                                "text": "Pretty soon I struck into a sort of path[…]. It twisted and turned,[…]and opened out into a big clear space like a lawn. And, back of the lawn, was a big, old-fashioned house, with piazzas stretching in front of it, and all blazing with lights."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "ead5862a-a119-4e70-b470-449747b11c26",
                                                "sense_id": "f392e96b-ef83-3164-9733-00d30270545b",
                                                "text": "T. S. Eliot suspects Mr. Pound’s philosophy of being antiquated. W. C. Williams finds his “versification still patterned after classic metres”; and, apropos of ‘feminolatry,’ is not the view of woman expressed by the Cantos older-fashioned than that of Siam and Abyssinia? knowledge of the femaleness of “chaos”, of the “octopus”, of “Our mulberry leaf, woman,” appertaining more to the Grand Turk than to a Roger Ascham?"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "c12f35ca-9a04-45c2-b298-7382dda5833d",
                                                "sense_id": "f392e96b-ef83-3164-9733-00d30270545b",
                                                "text": "Walter Wren & Co. were a china clay firm right enough, but much smaller and older-fashioned than CCC."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "f0e5b8c7-8d07-3284-a6ce-645c55574602",
                                        "entry_id": "0f822407-f74e-3586-bb6b-944b98803345",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Of a person, preferring the customs of earlier times and the old-style ways."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "19667686-40ec-4361-ac08-d69aba570a17",
                                                "sense_id": "f0e5b8c7-8d07-3284-a6ce-645c55574602",
                                                "text": "You can’t stay the night, because my parents are a bit old-fashioned."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "937c15ee-c552-499c-9a46-4646c8d34858",
                                                "sense_id": "f0e5b8c7-8d07-3284-a6ce-645c55574602",
                                                "text": "The people of Marken may almost be regarded as the oldest-fashioned in the world. They adhere to the same picturesque costume as was worn by their ancestors three hundred years ago, and their houses are built in the same primitive style as in those days."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "31d8128b-2716-4de2-8e48-fd25d927625b",
                                                "sense_id": "f0e5b8c7-8d07-3284-a6ce-645c55574602",
                                                "text": "It neither aims at, nor does it admit of, the gorgeousness of its predecessor; mainly, or at least partly, because it does not aim at or admit of that predecessor’s variety of rhythm. / In the respect with which alone we have to do, Steele is merely a more careless Addison, and Arbuthnot, in this as in others, is almost inseparable from Swift. Atterbury is slightly older-fashioned than the others, and nearer the Dryden group."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            },
                            {
                                "target_word": "old-fashioned",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "dbd0914c-2dc5-3ab2-af73-661c3b908fb1",
                                        "entry_id": "cb20013d-a49e-3f97-b0fb-1263b1b4e553",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A cocktail made by muddling sugar with bitters and adding whiskey or, less commonly, brandy, served with a twist of citrus rind."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "3bde2632-a013-407b-90f8-b3ae95d0f60f",
                                                "sense_id": "dbd0914c-2dc5-3ab2-af73-661c3b908fb1",
                                                "text": "Old John was mixing Old Fashioneds and every now and then he would turn and stare at the record case with an expression of great loathing."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "3a2da6d0-0ef8-4503-b3f2-6ae6d91b8413",
                                                "sense_id": "dbd0914c-2dc5-3ab2-af73-661c3b908fb1",
                                                "text": "Bond took a shower and changed and walked down the road and had two Bourbon old-fashioneds and the Chicken Dinner at $2.80 in the air-conditioned eating house on the corner that was as typical of ‘the American way of life’ as the motel."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "5282adc8-c488-4c0e-ad22-c2a77ae1c88c",
                                                "sense_id": "dbd0914c-2dc5-3ab2-af73-661c3b908fb1",
                                                "text": "At the end of the workday, the Trumans liked to have a cocktail before dinner. Shortly after they moved into the White House, Mrs. Truman rang for the butler, Alonzo Fields, one afternoon and ordered two old-fashioneds."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "b9f1696e-0aa4-3c2e-af09-7bb74bd40128",
                                        "entry_id": "cb20013d-a49e-3f97-b0fb-1263b1b4e553",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A type of doughnut with a cakelike consistency and a rough surface, usually made with cultured buttermilk and chemical leaven and fried at a lower temperature."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": []
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "a3211520-32cf-425e-8058-1200a7f1f8ad",
                        "source_entry_id": "42f639c0-017c-32a3-89e9-c86ceedc8db6",
                        "source_sense_id": "9927ccb6-5a1d-3fd1-be3a-9de362bdb142",
                        "target_lang_word": "passé",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "passé",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "27c6de78-c5ba-37af-9409-176b1682d415",
                                        "entry_id": "456f6a90-a0b6-3f9c-a805-32927a70f2b5",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Dated; out of style; old-fashioned."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "colloquial"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "cd386e55-3265-4137-b08f-d7198dc4696d",
                                                "sense_id": "27c6de78-c5ba-37af-9409-176b1682d415",
                                                "text": "Then, like side fringes, Smirnoff Ice and tights under denim shorts, smoking was suddenly passé – distasteful, even gross."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "4fd011d7-a0d6-40a5-8c0b-fafd8c7ebc5d",
                                                "sense_id": "27c6de78-c5ba-37af-9409-176b1682d415",
                                                "text": "I never thought you'd be a junkie, because heroin is so passé."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "5cf364c3-3332-411a-980d-69e9c96f659c",
                                                "sense_id": "27c6de78-c5ba-37af-9409-176b1682d415",
                                                "text": "We'll paint the town blue 'cause, baby, red is so passé."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "c1dc3f7e-9be2-4469-8d99-c64b64cf2351",
                                                "sense_id": "27c6de78-c5ba-37af-9409-176b1682d415",
                                                "text": "It is perhaps inevitable that a movement that was the height of fashion in the last decade would start to seem passé in this one. That’s how style works; the young and innovative distinguish themselves by breaking with the conventions of their predecessors."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "bb1e4652-3d4b-31d2-8ad7-5426eff1030e",
                                        "entry_id": "456f6a90-a0b6-3f9c-a805-32927a70f2b5",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Past one's prime; worn; faded."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "1340c23d-65cb-4504-9ebb-cc195fea71eb",
                                                "sense_id": "bb1e4652-3d4b-31d2-8ad7-5426eff1030e",
                                                "text": "The coaching stock is in general in a very passé condition, but the ex-royal saloon, though needing a coat of paint outside, as another photograph shows, is spotless inside."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            },
